#: ../pwntools/docs/source/constants.rst:7
msgid ":mod:`pwnlib.constants` --- Easy access to header file constants"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.constants:1
msgid "Module containing constants extracted from header files."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.constants:3
msgid ""
"The purpose of this module is to provide quick access to constants from "
"different architectures and operating systems."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.constants:6
msgid ""
"The constants are wrapped by a convenience class that allows accessing "
"the name of the constant, while performing all normal mathematical "
"operations on it."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.constants:11 pwnlib.constants:31
msgid "Example"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.constants:23
msgid ""
"The submodule ``freebsd`` contains all constants for FreeBSD, while the "
"constants for Linux have been split up by architecture."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.constants:26
msgid ""
"The variables of the submodules will be \"lifted up\" by setting the "
":data:`pwnlib.context.arch` or :data:`pwnlib.context.os` in a manner "
"similar to what happens in :mod:`pwnlib.shellcraft`."
msgstr ""

